KEPT.poke(steal h) keeps a view of 'm' in the global 'KEPT', which every routine reaches, and the build can't compare those later uses with where that view's place is given back: keep an Addr there (the view's .to[Addr](), turned back with .to[@T?]() and a when), make the field an &E? when one holder keeps the value, or hand the view as an argument to the routines that use it
